### ZR/ZF scope correction

The independently audited ZR/ZF theorem is a theorem about the **nonisolated positive-contact core** `V`, not the full source. With `v=|V|`,

\[
\ker\Omega_V=\operatorname{span}\{\mathbf1,P_x|_V,P_y|_V\},
\qquad
\operatorname{rank}R_{C\cup H}[V]=2v-3,
\]

and therefore

\[
e+h\ge2v-2,
\qquad
h\ge\delta\ge\lceil D\rceil.
\]

Contact-isolated source points remain in the global configuration. Extending the core stress matrix by zero rows and columns creates additional kernel directions. `C-ZRF-FULL-SOURCE` remains rejected. No bound on the isolated source population follows from ZR/ZF.

