### Exact remaining split

The global §§79--80 dichotomy still leaves two real branches.

1. **Macroscopic-container branch.** One actual internal inactive chamber or exterior cap has quadratic source population/area with only `O(D)` perimeter/slack. For an internal chamber, canonical hull stability and deep matching give a protected isolate hull and isolate-only blocker graph. Proof-only §95 shows contact creation alone is not a force-transfer theorem. A closure must force an exact unit triangle, alter or replace the old diameter-carrying core, or construct a same-cardinality strict sub-`D` source.

2. **Full-core branch.** The new canonical diameter-budget floor first removes every
   survivor sequence with \(\liminf\mu_D<1\), and
   `C-FULLCORE-FLOOR-ENDPOINT-EXCLUSION` removes convergence to the exact
   train-coupled endpoint \(\mu_{\rm TC}\), where
   \[
   \mu_D={e_{BB}+2s_C-3(d_H+s_Z)\over D}.
   \]
   The remaining full-core regime still has only the necessary
   \(\liminf\mu_D\ge1.6375621841815\ldots\) by the loaded-chord/train floor; the
   endpoint exclusion supplies a non-explicit qualitative gap above
   \(\mu_{\rm TC}\), but no numerical/effective gap or upper bound. It still has
   the two compatible source-level scales.
   - On one actual carrier, §§120--121 convert train anisotropy into local detour and then into local non-rhombic area currency.
   - Globally across the harmonic tiling, §§122--123 force a linear aggregate detour and pay the exceptional-face portion by the single loaded-hull scalar `e_BB-k`.

   The clean remaining aggregate target is therefore
   \[
   \sum_r(L_r-2d_r)
   \]
   coupled to `e_BB-k` and the global diameter graph. A closure needs a sharp enough upper bound on this same currency, a source-preserving deformation, or an exact unit triangle. Further carrier-decimal optimization is secondary unless it creates such a source-level implication.

